From be5c5571f7257eeda7c070dbf8c9e7137841ac1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:03:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): lanes second review: forced decompose, agent
 shells, default-lane gate, link release order [daveey]

- a held card is refused by decompose even with --force
- created_by=user counts only from a human shell (no agent session), not just the absence of a worker card
- a tenant that names no lane is gated as the default lane
- link release needs a runnable waiter (todo/ready/running/review), which also covers a waiter being created held
- held excludes cards released by promote/unblock/admit; admit records the lane whose budget it spends
- self-work intake resolves the project repository before matching; shares must be finite
- a config backend outage (SystemExit) no longer escapes; the malformed-config warning logs once per error

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
